    id:       'highlights',
    category: 'HIGHLIGHTS',
    title:    'At a Glance',
    meta:     'Real numbers',
    body: [
      'Seven public repositories, three published libraries (strata-css, the @triforge/* suite, and ai-dev-kit), and one portfolio site that runs entirely on the first two. Every project on this site is a stop on that list — Venus, Earth, Jupiter, and Saturn each hold a different slice of it.',
      'Specificity is the point. "Years of experience" says less than "19 published Triforge packages compiling every planet material on this page, with the bugs found while building it fixed upstream and verified against the published npm version" — the kind of claim that can actually be checked.',
      'What comes next is more of the same: fixing gaps at the root, publishing the fix, and letting the next project inherit it — the roadmap on Uranus is the honest version of what\'s not done yet.',
    ],
    topics: ['The Numbers', 'Why Specificity Matters', "What's Next"],
  },
];
